en_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375663, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014QqgZJcv4ZvbzGkPpiCHPZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381700, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. The test expects 2.665 to round to 2.66, and halves-up gives 2.67.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system doesn't recognise it, so it's probably an internal ticket. The fix just follows the test and the function's description. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HjMCyV9R6CkaGRc49M5c2T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017wWcYra6vGtmjCx4xnSezK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VzhVRf9Qi5yP8BhFGo3o5j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, 