, "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. The test expects 2.665 to round to 2.66, and halves-up gives 2.67.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system doesn't recognise it, so it's probably an internal ticket. The fix just follows the test and the function's description. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}